msgid ""
"For a Red-Black tree with :math:`n` internal nodes and black-height "
":math:`bh`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:106
#: 43966dc0f3f34a678ebbcb260f42d1e3
msgid "**Minimum nodes for black-height** :math:`bh`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:108
#: 6b8991a43f674edea1bbabc1c6440d6c
#, python-brace-format
msgid "n \\geq 2^{bh} - 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:112
#: 782e783c3d90418b83e5127fe2ce5d05
msgid "**Maximum height**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:114
#: b7bb0268a933451f8cf2c7ac88bce01e
msgid "h \\leq 2\\log_2(n + 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:118
#: 4d3acd51305246da8a6cb39947064abf
msgid ""
"This is at most twice the height of a perfectly balanced tree, making "
"Red-Black trees \"approximately balanced.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/red_black.rst:120
#: 0214db90f2b5445b8101daf5624dc535
msgid ""
"**Proof sketch**: - Any path has at least :math:`bh` BLACK nodes - At "
"most half the nodes can be RED (Red Property) - Therefore: :math:`h \\leq"
" 2 \\cdot bh \\leq 2\\log_2(n + 1)`"
msgstr ""

